   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the mental hygiene law, in relation to directing the\ncommissioner of mental health to publish information on the office of mental\nhealth website about the mental illness anti-stigma distinctive license plates",
    "basePrintNo": "S9057",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9057-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §7.09, Ment Hyg L",
    "lawSection": "Mental Hygiene Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9057\n\nSPONSOR: BROUK\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the mental hygiene law, in relation to directing the\ncommissioner of mental health to publish information on the office of\nmental health website about the mental illness anti-stigma distinctive\nlicense plates\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis directs the commissioner of mental health to publish information\nabout the mental illness anti-stigma distinctive license plates on the\noffice of mental health website.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of the bill would amend the mental hygiene law to add a new\nSubdivision (m) to Section 7.09 requiring the commissioner to publish on\nthe website of the Office of Mental Health information regarding the\nmental illness anti-stigma distinctive license plate.\n\nSection two of the bill provides timeframe for taking effect.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nChapter 228 of the Laws of 2017 established the mental illness anti-\nstigma license plate. Currently, the license plate can be ordered from\nthe Department of Motor Vehicles, and twenty-five dollars from each\nplate purchased supports the Mental Illness Anti-Stigma Fund.\n\nThis bill directs the Office of Mental Health to publish information\nconcerning the plate on their website in order to raise awareness and\npublicize its availability.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nBUDGET IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to state\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
